{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "our support agent (ADK, deployed on Cloud Run) keeps getting customers pasting full card numbers and sometimes their account passwords into the chat. legal flagged that this stuff is showing up in Cloud Logging and in the session history we persist to Firestore. I need a before_model_callback / after_model_callback setup that redacts PII before it hits Gemini and before it gets saved or logged, plus scrubs tool call args. Should I be using Sensitive Data Protection (DLP) for this or Model Armor or both? Also what APIs/IAM/templates do I need to provision — we're terraforming everything. deadline is end of next sprint."},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Quick q. Building a health intake assistant with google-adk. Users type symptoms, meds, DOB, insurance IDs etc. I want: 1) mask that before it's sent to the model and in our logs, 2) screen prompts + responses with Model Armor for jailbreak/sensitive data, 3) not break streaming (we stream partial responses to the frontend over SSE). How do I filter the streamed chunks without buffering the whole reply? Rough architecture + GCP setup pls."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "Hey — security review on our ADK agent came back and they want the Gemini API key and the Postgres password out of the .env file we bake into the container image. We're on GKE. What's the cleanest way to load those at runtime, and how do I rotate them without redeploying the agent? Kinda urgent, review is Thursday.", "needs_instead": "Secrets management for the application's own credentials (e.g., Secret Manager with Workload Identity on GKE, rotation strategy), not detecting or masking sensitive data that users type into the agent chat."}
]}
